@startuml
title CD-01 - SkillSwap domain model
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
hide empty members
class Student {
 - id: Long
 - name: String
 - email: String {unique}
 - passwordHash: String
 - bio: String
 - learningInterests: String
 + updateProfile(name, bio, interests)
}
class SkillListing {
 - id: Long
 - title: String
 - description: String
 - availabilityNote: String
 - active: boolean
 + edit(title, description, note)
 + archive()
}
class SkillCategory {
 - id: Long
 - name: String
}
class SessionRequest {
 - id: Long
 - startAt: Instant
 - endAt: Instant
 - meetingDetails: String
 - message: String
 - status: SessionStatus
 + accept(): void
 + decline(): void
 + cancel(): void
 + complete(): void
}
enum SessionStatus {
 PENDING
 ACCEPTED
 DECLINED
 CANCELLED
 COMPLETED
}
Student "1" -- "0..*" SkillListing : owns
SkillCategory "1" -- "0..*" SkillListing : categorizes
SkillListing "1" -- "0..*" SessionRequest : requests for
Student "1" -- "0..*" SessionRequest : learner
SessionRequest ..> SessionStatus : status
note bottom of SessionRequest
 Tutor = listing.owner. A learner cannot book their own listing.
 Each request has exactly one listing and one learner.
 Times and participants are immutable after creation.
 SessionService checks permissions, time guards and booking conflicts.
 Domain methods guard the allowed status transitions.
end note
@enduml
